3. ENTERPRISE USE AND COMMERCIAL USE

"Enterprise" means a for-profit business or organization of any size,
including a company, partnership, sole proprietorship, startup, affiliate,
or other entity carrying on business for commercial advantage.

"Enterprise Use" means use of the Material by an Enterprise, or work using
the Material on behalf of, at the direction of, under contract to, or for the
business benefit of an Enterprise. This includes internal research,
benchmarking, evaluation, employee or contractor work, development, testing,
training, integration, deployment, and production. No revenue, distribution,
external customer, minimum company size, or production launch is required.

An individual employed by an Enterprise may use the free grant for genuinely
personal, independent noncommercial research that is not work for or for the
business benefit of that Enterprise. Employment alone does not prohibit
personal study. Enterprise-directed or enterprise-sponsored work is not
personal study merely because it is performed outside normal working hours.

"Commercial Use" means use of the Material in connection with a product,
service, paid application, consulting engagement, commercial offering, or
other activity undertaken for commercial advantage or monetary compensation,
whether conducted by an Enterprise, an individual, or a nonprofit entity.
An ordinary salary, student stipend, or public or nonprofit research grant
does not by itself make otherwise eligible noncommercial teaching or academic
research Commercial Use. This clarification does not exempt any Enterprise
Use, including enterprise-sponsored or enterprise-directed work.
Research funded or commissioned for an Enterprise's business purposes is
Enterprise Use even when an academic institution performs it.

3A. Limited Hiring and Engagement Review

Notwithstanding the Enterprise Use and Commercial Use exclusions in section 2, the separate-license and payment requirements in section 4, and the purpose and recipient-license limitations in section 5, the Licensor grants a worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free copyright license for the limited review described in this section. No separate written license or licensing fee is required for that review.

Prospective employers or clients, and individuals directly participating in their hiring or engagement decision, may review Material publicly released by the Licensor under this license solely to decide whether to employ Timothy Paul Bielec or engage Timothy Paul Bielec or TASUMER MAF to provide professional services. They may inspect the published Material, discuss it within that review group, and prepare internal assessments for that decision. This permission does not authorize evaluation of the Material for adoption, integration, licensing, or operational use by the prospective employer or client.

For this review, reviewers may make necessary local copies of the public release and run only its unmodified, publicly supplied examples, using their supplied sample inputs, on devices under their control. Temporary build and runtime files necessary to run those examples are permitted. This exception does not authorize source modification, use with reviewers’ own datasets, operation as a shared or hosted service, or any other execution. Reviewers may also use demonstrations hosted by the Licensor and expressly made available for hiring or engagement review.

Copies permitted by this section may be shared only among individuals directly participating in the same review, with this license and applicable copyright, attribution, and third-party notices retained. Each participant receives permission directly from the Licensor under these terms. No public redistribution or wider internal distribution is authorized by this exception. When the review ends, copies made solely under this exception must be deleted. A brief internal record of the assessment or decision may be retained if it contains no source code or substantial reproduction of the Material.

This exception grants no permission for enterprise or commercial research and development, product evaluation, independent benchmarking, employee or contractor training, AI or machine-learning training, fine-tuning, model evaluation, dataset construction, modification, integration, deployment, production, or incorporation into products, services, or client deliverables. It does not authorize using a hiring or engagement review as a substitute for obtaining a license for those activities.

Material, substantial excerpts, and review copies may not be uploaded, pasted, submitted, or otherwise provided to external AI tools, coding assistants, model providers, or AI analysis services under this exception without the Licensor’s prior written approval of the specific service and use. Such approval does not, by itself, authorize training or any other activity outside this section’s review purpose.

No ownership, patent, trademark, confidential-source, reserved-corpus, or other rights beyond the copyright permission expressly stated here are granted. The Licensor is not required to disclose private source code, unpublished material, proprietary information, or other material omitted from the public release. This section creates no employment, services, assignment, or additional licensing commitment.

The restrictions in this section apply only to permission granted by this section. They do not reduce rights independently available under section 2, a separate agreement, applicable third-party licenses, or applicable law, including the rights preserved in section 6. All other applicable provisions of this license remain in effect.

